# Scalability & Future Plan

## 1. Introduction

The Script-Controlled ACL solution can be extended in the future to support additional users, roles, branches, tables, and security requirements.

## 2. Additional Branches

More branch values can be added to the system when required.

For example, additional academic or organizational branches can be introduced and included in the access-control conditions.

## 3. Additional Roles

New roles can be created for different categories of users.

This allows the system to support more detailed permission requirements.

## 4. Additional Tables

The same ACL-based approach can be applied to other ServiceNow tables.

This can help maintain consistent security controls across multiple applications and datasets.

## 5. Advanced Conditions

The ACL logic can be extended to evaluate additional record fields and user-related conditions.

This can provide more detailed control over record access.

## 6. Automated Testing

Automated testing can be introduced to verify ACL behavior for different users, roles, operations, and record conditions.

This can reduce manual testing effort and improve consistency.

## 7. Future Integration

The solution can potentially be integrated with other ServiceNow applications and workflows where controlled record access is required.

## 8. Long-Term Scope

Future improvements may include:

* More detailed role-based permissions
* Additional field-based restrictions
* Automated security testing
* Integration with other ServiceNow modules
* Centralized access-control management

## 9. Conclusion

The project provides a foundation that can be expanded as the organization's access-control requirements grow. The modular ACL approach makes it possible to introduce additional security rules without redesigning the entire solution.
